it's the end of the year so it's time to  take a look back on the best of the best  from the last 12 months here are the  five best PlayStation games of 2022 as  selected by Gamespot as well as five  honorable mentions that you can't afford  to miss  [Music]  [Applause]  PlayStations right at the end of the  year is God of War Ragnarok the highly  anticipated follow-up to 2018's God of  War in Ragnarok Kratos and his son  atreus are up against their deadliest  foe yet the end of the world itself but  that's not all with both fearful of a  prophecy that Kratos will die at the end  of their Adventure Father and Son must  learn to accept each other for who they  are and learning that loving someone  deeply means that eventually you might  have to let them go Ragnarok tells a  heart-wrenching story trust me you'll  cry a couple of times and its combat is  as frenetic and crunchy as ever with  both Kratos and atreus slashing through  anyone who dares to try and get in their  way with unmatched brutality whether  they be run-of-the-mill draggers or even  the Norse gods themselves God of War  Ragnarok earned a 9 out of 10 in our  review with Timor Hussein saying God of  War ragnarok's most impressive  achievements are its exploration of loss  and love grief and growth determinism  and Defiance it's an astoundingly  well-written game that deconstructs the  mythology of Norse gods and rebuilds it  as an odyssey about families  stray isn't just the game that we fell  in love with it's the one that our cats  fell in love with too affectionately  known as the cat game stray went viral  this summer when people were posting  videos of their own pets reacting to the  game's adorable fluffy protagonist stray  is a puzzle Adventure game where you  take on the role of a stray cat who has  been separated from its family with the  help of a handy drone named B12 you  navigate through a dilapidated City  that's full of robots run away from  Aliens and get up to a lot of cat  Mischief we gave stray a 9 out of 10  with reviewer Alessandra Barbosa  specifically calling out that a lot of  the enjoyment throughout stray's run  time comes from how well each scenario  is designed for the abilities of its  feline hero stray expertly embodies the  abilities of its feline protagonist to  create a captivating puzzle Adventure in  an engrossing post-apocalyptic world  Horizon forbidden West launched at the  beginning of 2022 and as the sequel to  2017's Horizon zero Dawn it picks up  protagonist eloy's quest to save the  world you know that small job after  defeating the Rogue Hades AI at the end  of zero Dawn the Planet needs a little  more help to recover completely a  mysterious blight is sweeping across the  world and so Eloy must gather allies to  find some ancient Tech to set things  straight if you enjoyed the original  there's plenty for you to enjoy in its  sequel from eloy's Motley Crew who are  helping her fix the world to more  interesting and varied side quests set  in locations like San Francisco and Las  Vegas our reviewer Phil hornshaw gave it  an 8 out of 10 saying that Horizon  forbidden West sometimes packs in so  much that it gets in its own way but the  many well-drawn characters populating  its quests keep it compelling  sifu is a game that will truly test your  might as its clever fighting mechanics  are easy to grasp but tough to master  upon death you revive but with a Twist  you're a few years older with age comes  more strength but less life in your  health bar and getting too old ends the  game the highlight of sifu is its combat  a dance of dodging blocking and  attacking but only when the moment is  right our review at Richard Wakeling  called sifu an excellent modern beat em  up with deep combat mechanics and a  fascinating aging system that sets it  apart from its contemporaries by  altering the way you progress from one  chapter to the next he gave it a 9 out  of 10.  there are many reasons that naughty  dog's 2013 title The Last of Us has  endured as a classic for all these years  it's an emotionally gutting story told  through fantastic performances that  still resonates with players today  following its PS3 and PS4 releases and  with an HBO series on the horizon  Naughty Dog work to bring the game to  PlayStation 5 in 2022 not content with  just adding a visual overhaul Naughty  Dog added a bunch of new features to  this Edition including new game modes  display modes skins and visual filters  new trophies and crucially a whole host  of fantastic accessibility features so  more people can play The Last of Us Part  One sadly is missing the original game's  multiplayer mode but our reviewer Jake  Decker said The Last of Us Part 1  manages to tell a harrowing story of  loss and Redemption that still holds up  despite some of its dated level design  those were games what's 5 best  PlayStation games of 2022 but since  you've been good this year here are five  more  speaking of naughty dog it makes another  appearance on this list with the  Uncharted Legacy of Thieves collection  it bundles together Uncharted 4 and Lost  Legacy and both games have been updated  for PS5 so they feature dual Sims haptic  feedback quicker loading performance and  Performance Plus modes as well as 3D  audio Uncharted 4 one of the games  included in this collection earned a  rare 10 out of 10 from us back in 2016  with Mike mahadi calling out the game's  cinematography in particular claiming  that both in cutscenes and out it  amplifies The Wonder of its gorgeous  World Lost Legacy is a fantastic  Standalone Adventure that caps off the  whole Saga and is well worth your time  ghost wire Tokyo is the latest game from  Tango Gameworks the studio founded by  Master of horror Shinji makami while  ghostwire certainly leans into the  supernatural it's not full of Spooks  making for an enjoyable adventure around  a desolate Tokyo that submerged in fog  as Akito with help from KK a spirit  who's inhabiting his body it's up to you  to find out what's going on while its  side missions are a little inconsistent  its open world is beautiful and fun to  explore thanks to the game's truly  unique combat system in our 8 out of 10  review Richard Wakeling said that  ghostwire Tokyo's sheer creativity and  attention to detail exhibited throughout  constantly shine through  it wouldn't be a PlayStation best off  list without one of the platform's most  well-known franchises Gran Turismo the  latest gt7 launched earlier this year  earning a number of high review scores  including an 8 out of 10 from us with  reviewer Alex [ __ ] praising the game's  stunning visuals customization options  handling and load times while the core  game is great it's had a bit of a bumpy  go over the past few months with  controversies over its handling of  microtransactions online issues and  criticism over its roster however the  core racing experience is still  enjoyable and we think that earns it a  spot as one of our best PlayStation  games of the year  what would a skating game be like if the  main character had a gun you may find  yourself asking well Wonder no longer  because rollerdrome answers that very  specific question for you the latest  from olly olly World developers roll 7  launched earlier this year and it's a  single player roller skating game where  you balance maintaining momentum pulling  off tricks and taking out enemies that  spawn in the skate parks you're  practicing in it sounds like a lot to  keep track of but trust us you'll be  hitting that flow State and those score  multipliers in no time in his 8 out of  10 review Phil honshaw wrote developer  roll 7 excellently mixes high scoring  skating gameplay with shooter ideas to  make a hybrid game that's tough to put  down  of course I couldn't finish this list  without mentioning Elden ring the  overall Gamespot game of the year it may  not be a console exclusive but it's a  must-have regardless of platform it's an  open world done in from software fashion  so it's filled with wonder Discovery and  of course a whole host of enemies that  are ready to fight you at every turn in  his 10 out of 10 review Tamar Hussein  wrote in a genre that has become wrought  with bloated and over-designed games  Elden ring is defiantly contrarian in  almost every way it will go down in  history as one of the all-time greats a  Triumph in design and creativity and an  open world game that distinguishes  itself for what it doesn't do as much as  what it does and if that doesn't sell  you I'm not sure what will  those were all picks for the best  PlayStation games of 2022 if you want to  know the best Xbox switch and PC games  of the year make sure to subscribe to  Gamespot on YouTube or check out  gamespot.com we also have an in-depth  video on our game of the year Elden ring  and why it got that coveted prize you  can find me on Twitter at Lucy James  games and I'll see you next time  [Music]
 

